cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use WulfPeak in your research, please cite this software."
title: "WulfPeak"
type: software
version: "0.2.2"
date-released: "2026-08-10"

authors:
  - family-names: "Kudoh"
    given-names: "Fuki"
    affiliation: "Tokyo Metropolitan Institute of Medical Science"
    orcid: "https://orcid.org/0000-0001-8986-4216"

abstract: >-
  WulfPeak is a lightweight command-line pipeline for ChIP-seq
  preprocessing and analysis. It provides FASTQ quality control,
  trimming, Bowtie2 alignment, BAM processing, normalized BigWig
  generation, MultiQC reporting, resumable execution, sample-level
  parallelism, and reproducible provenance tracking.

keywords:
  - ChIP-seq
  - epigenomics
  - bioinformatics
  - Bowtie2
  - deepTools
  - MultiQC
  - chromatin

license: "MIT"

repository-code: "https://github.com/Fuki-Kudoh/WulfPeak"
url: "https://github.com/Fuki-Kudoh/WulfPeak"
